 "name": "rheumatology conditions overview",
 "width": 1724,
 "title": "Rheumatology conditions at a glance: one swollen joint is septic or crystal arthritis; two or more joints are sorted by the synovial fluid and serology into osteoarthritis, rheumatoid arthritis, spondyloarthritis, connective tissue disease and, in a child, juvenile idiopathic arthritis; with no swollen joints, several organs point to vasculitis and pain all over to polymyalgia rheumatica or fibromyalgia; each branch names the chart that covers it",
